# ============================================================================
# ONRECORD STUDIO - GLOBAL GITIGNORE PROFILE
# Target Ecosystem: Tauri v2 + Rust Backend + React TypeScript Frontend
# ============================================================================

# 1. OS & Native Desktop Cache Omissions
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
Icon?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes

# 2. Frontend Dependencies & Compilers Build Caches
node_modules/
dist/
dist-tauri/
.vite/
.eslintcache
*.tsbuildinfo
# package-lock.json is intentionally NOT ignored: this is an application, and a committed
# lockfile is what makes `npm ci` and `npm audit` reproducible for every contributor.
yarn.lock
pnpm-lock.yaml

# 3. Native macOS Rust Backend Compilation Artifacts
src-tauri/target/
# Cargo.lock is committed for the same reason as package-lock.json. The previous rule named
# `src-tauri/Cargo.lock`, which never matched anything: this is a workspace, so the lockfile is
# written to the repository root instead.

# Tauri-generated ACL schemas, rebuilt on every build.
src-tauri/gen/schemas/
# Materialized from reviewed templates by `npm run prepare:app-store`; these contain the Apple
# team identifier, provisioning profile, and export-compliance answer for one release account.
src-tauri/Entitlements.appstore.plist
src-tauri/Info.appstore.plist
src-tauri/AppStore.provisionprofile

# 4. Local App Data Caches, SQLite DBs, & Extracted Public Documents
# Protects investigator database indices and scraped municipal files from being leaked to public repositories.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
.onrecord_studio_cache/
nextrequest_downloads/
downloads/
onrecord-studio/downloads/
onrecord-studio/nextrequest_downloads/

# 5. IDE Configurations & Environments
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
.idea/
.vscode/
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.swp
